            <ArticleTitle>Shallow left anterior oblique right coronary angiography: technique and applications.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>604-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A &quot;new&quot; shallow left anterior oblique view of the right coronary artery allows better visualization of the distal vessel in selected patients. This paper describes the angiographic technique; retrospective data suggest that the view is useful in approximately 20% of patients. An illustrative case is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
